# Findings `make scan-alpha` accepts in the alpha server's third-party images, and why. Only that target reads this
# file (--ignorefile), so the API and gateway scans still report the same IDs if they ever show up there. The form is
# the root .trivyignore's (docs/security/dependencies.md 3장): the reason above each ID and an expiry, after which the
# scan fails again and the finding is looked at anew.
#
# golang.org/x/net/html: crafted HTML makes the parser spend unbounded time. caddy:2.11.9 (Go 1.27.3, x/net 0.60.0)
# is the newest Caddy image and links the package, but the alpha Caddy never parses HTML: it proxies bytes to the API
# and the gateway and serves one JSON file. Bump Caddy when an image built with x/net 0.62.0 or later is out.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-17
# zlib's gz* file-writing API (gz_vacate) in the PostgreSQL image's Debian zlib1g. The server links zlib only for the
# deflate stream API, and the one tool run in this container, pg_dump in the custom format (db-dump.sh), compresses
# through that API too, not through gzopen/gzwrite. postgres:16.16 still ships the same package; bump when an image
# with zlib1g 1.3.1-1+deb13u1 is out.
CVE-2026-85091 exp:2026-12-17
